In the United States, cases have already been reported where lawyers submitted briefs generated by AI that contained "non-existent, fabricated judicial precedents (hallucinations)" to courts, resulting in penalties. Similarly, medical AIs have derived misdiagnoses due to racial biases and data imbalances. Unless humans strictly audit the correctness of outputs—as they do with dictionaries and calculators—there is nothing but risk in domains involving human lives and destinies.

Digital Kleptomania and the Critical Point of Dependence:

The act of plundering the topology (framework) of others' copyrighted works with a single button press and laundering it as one's own output constitutes, from psychiatric and socio-psychological perspectives, an extremely malicious dependence and criminal pathology: "digital kleptomania," which boundlessly consumes and steals the intellectual property of others, and "digital stalking," where an individual obsessively forces the system to output the specific style or voice of a particular creator. Interlocking with gacha addiction (the hacking of the brain's reward system), this has reached an "irreversible epidemic (critical point)" that degrades the cognitive capacity of society as a whole.

